    "updated_at": "2021-02-08T21:43:46Z",
    "body": "Thank you for the suggestions.  I unchecked \"Use Unicode version 9+ widths\" and it worked \\o/\r\n\r\nBefore that, I tried `set fish_emoji_width 2`, but it didn't solve the issue. I also tried to set fish_emoji_width to 1 and 0, no change. I am using Fira Code Nerd Font v2.1.0 preset as a fallback to MonoLisa (see picture 1). I tried to put it as the default font and it didn't solve the issue. Should I use another font? Do you guys have a suggestion?\r\n\r\nAlso, FYI, I tried all options of the Unicode uniformization form without success. What worked was to uncheck \"Use Unicode version 9+ widths\". However, there is no space anymore between the Gopher and the version number (see picture 2)\r\n\r\nI am not reproducing this issue with NodeJS. But I can reproduce it with Python, OCaml, Rust\r\n\r\npicture 1:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/702227/107282615-23c6e800-6a53-11eb-95a0-cd166808799e.png)\r\n\r\npicture 2:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/702227/107283039-be272b80-6a53-11eb-8714-4bc371ea3438.png)\r\n",
